			<div class="content" id="post-content-4477323">
									

<p>My second mainlist article, second time posting it. I've made some rewriting and topical additions, the previous lack of which led to unnecessary confusion.</p>
<p>I'd like to thank <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/someauthordude" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5643926); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5643926&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579791028" alt="someauthordude" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5643926)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/someauthordude" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5643926); return false;">someauthordude</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=776854&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579791028" alt="Tanhony" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=776854)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;">Tanhony</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/keon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(154549); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=154549&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579791028" alt="keon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=154549)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/keon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(154549); return false;">keon</a></span> for giving me feedback.</p>
<p>This is based around an earlier idea of mine in which a cartoon Foundation contained a normal human. The idea felt extremely flat though. I instead wanted to have a single object display multiple effects: some small inanimate object, maybe with a dial so that It'll be easy to accommodate any number of possible effects I could think of.</p>
<p>All images in this article are taken by me, feature myself, and have been edited by myself using software which I legally own (Sony Vegas Pro and Sketchbook Pro, respectively). As such, I'm releasing them under the Creative Commons 3.0 licence.</p>
<p>The extent of the actual effects of SCP-4832 is intentionally left ambiguous. My original headcanon with the first iteration of this article was that SCP-4832 changes the appearance of the entire universe. This led to some strange implications though, and my current headcanon is that SCP-4832 only changes its immediate surroundings.</p>

